---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Heredita — About Us">
  <main class="container">
    <section class="about-hero reveal">
      <img src="/assets/heredita-logo-full.webp" alt="Heredita" style="width:clamp(180px,22vw,260px); margin-bottom:8px;" />
      <h1 class="tilt-l">About <span class="accent">Heredita</span></h1>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size:1.12rem; max-width:640px; margin:0 auto;">
        A collaborative chalkboard for people who have thoughts about alternate history.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="chalk-card reveal" style="margin-top:28px;">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Who are you?</h2>
      <p>Heredita is made by four of us: Whirl, Digi, Legi and Hilmi. We met on the internet to make this!</p>
      <p>We wanted somewhere history, geography and politics people could roleplay a country without it turning into a strategy game. They're fun, you should play them sometimes, but it's not what we want to do.</p>
      <p>What we <b>want</b> to do is make a game where everyone can roleplay and have a blast doing it.</p>
      <p>The part we care most about isn't the game as much as it is making a community who enjoys it and uses it for their own roleplay ideas.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size:.88rem; margin-bottom:0; max-width: 100%;">Heredita is operated by Anywhere Connection Corporation. That's also just the four of us, but we made a company!</p>
    </section>

    <div class="section-title reveal"><h2>What you do</h2></div>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="chalk-card reveal delay-1">
        <h3><span class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4.2 19.8 8 18.4 19.1 7.3a2.1 2.1 0 0 0-3-3L5 15.4z"/><path d="M14.6 5.6 17.8 8.8"/></svg></span> Roleplay anything </h3>
        <p>You roleplay what you want to do, see if it works, and draw it. You could found a city, or put a nation back on the map that hasn't been there since 1795.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chalk-card reveal delay-2">
        <h3><span class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3.6" y="3.6" width="16.8" height="16.8" rx="3.4"/><circle cx="8.6" cy="8.6" r="1.2" fill="currentColor"/><circle cx="15.4" cy="15.4" r="1.2" fill="currentColor"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1.2" fill="currentColor"/></svg></span> The chat stays honest</h3>
        <p>Annexations are roleplayed in front of everyone. Nobody loses a province to a formula, and nobody wins one from one either.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chalk-card reveal delay-3">
        <h3><span class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 20.4V5.2a1.6 1.6 0 0 1 1.6-1.6h9.2a1.6 1.6 0 0 1 1.6 1.6v3.2"/><path d="M5 8.4h13.4v12h-12a1.4 1.4 0 0 1-1.4-1.4z"/></svg></span> Make the country yours</h3>
        <p>Flag, government, reforms, everything. Put it on the map and see if it'll survive... or better yet, <b>make it</b> survive.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chalk-card reveal delay-1">
        <h3><span class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.8"/><path d="M12 6.6V12l3.6 2.2"/></svg></span> Change history</h3>
        <p>Pick maps from all eras, alter a single decision, and play out what follows. Have fun diverging from history.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chalk-card reveal delay-2">
        <h3><span class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20.6 14.6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7.4l-4 4V5.4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h13.2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"/></svg></span> Talk it out</h3>
        <p>Chat is in the same window as the map, so treaties and wars happen while you're looking at the thing you're fighting over.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chalk-card reveal delay-3">
        <h3><span class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.8"/><path d="M3.4 12h17.2"/><path d="M12 3.2a14 14 0 0 1 0 17.6 14 14 0 0 1 0-17.6z"/></svg></span> Run your own game</h3>
        <p>Host a server, write house rules, keep a thousand-year campaign going. That's always something you can do, and we'll help you do it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="chalk-card reveal" style="margin-top:24px;">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Why not (my favorite strategy game)?</h2>
      <p>
        Strategy games are great, you should play them. There's definitely something different about roleplaying your country though, instead of playing a pre-determined strategy game. Roleplaying everything lets you make your country do just about anything you can justify, and that's fun.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="chalk-card reveal" style="margin-top:24px;">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Why not Pax Historia?</h2>
      <p>
        Pax Historia is a pretty neat concept, but you can also just prompt inject it. This is between real people, so the AI isn't focused on you. <small class="muted">(There isn't even an AI.)</small> You can also talk to others in our community, host games between your friends, and do whatever else suits your fancy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="chalk-card reveal" style="margin-top:18px; text-align:center;">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Come draw something</h2>
      <p class="muted text-center">The playtest is free and open, and you don't need an account to try it.</p>
      <a href="https://app.heredita.net/app/" data-play class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:6px;">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><polygon points="7 4 20 12 7 20"/></svg>
        Open the playtest
      </a>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
